sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Operator as Platform Operator<br/>(KF Trainer / Kueue / KubeRay)
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant TrainingPod as Training Pod<br/>(Runtime/Universal Image)
    participant Worker as Worker Pods<br/>(OpenMPI Peers)
    participant MinIO as MinIO Storage<br/>9000/TCP
    participant NFS as NFS Server<br/>2049/TCP
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS

    Note over User,Route: Training Job Submission Flow

    User->>K8sAPI: Submit TrainingJob / RayJob CR<br/>kubectl / SDK
    K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event: new training resource
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create Pod specs with<br/>training image + config
    K8sAPI->>TrainingPod: Schedule master pod
    K8sAPI->>Worker: Schedule worker pods

    Note over TrainingPod,Worker: Multi-Node Training Coordination (OpenMPI)

    TrainingPod->>Worker: SSH connection (port 2222)<br/>uid_entrypoint.sh configures sshd
    Worker-->>TrainingPod: MPI rank registration
    TrainingPod->>Worker: mpirun distributed training<br/>PyTorch DDP / DeepSpeed

    Note over TrainingPod,NFS: Storage Access

    TrainingPod->>MinIO: Download training data<br/>S3 API (port 9000)<br/>Auth: AWS credentials from Secret
    MinIO-->>TrainingPod: Training dataset
    TrainingPod->>NFS: Read/write shared checkpoints<br/>NFS mount (port 2049/TCP)
    NFS-->>TrainingPod: Checkpoint data
    Worker->>NFS: Write gradient/checkpoint data
    TrainingPod->>MinIO: Upload trained model<br/>S3 PUT (port 9000)

    Note over User,Route: External Access (Examples)

    User->>Route: Access MinIO Console<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS termination
    Route->>MinIO: Forward to 9001/TCP (console)<br/>or 9000/TCP (API)

    Note over TrainingPod,K8sAPI: Status Reporting

    TrainingPod->>K8sAPI: Update training status<br/>kubernetes Python client
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Status change event
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Update TrainingJob status
